CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^\[printf\.assigns\.\d+\] line \d+ Check that \*p is assignable: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^Invariant check failed
--
Loop assigns inference inlines the callees of loop_fn before loop_fn's calls
are instrumented. When printf has already been instrumented, the arguments of
the call need a placeholder for its write set parameter: otherwise &a binds to
the write set parameter and 0 to p, so that the inferred loop assigns miss a.
